%% G. End-to-end sequence — v1.1 two-track session
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User
  participant Web as Next.js UI
  participant API as FastAPI /api/v1
  participant Intake as intake (graph, readiness, priority)
  participant Docs as documents (PyMuPDF, reader, verifier)
  participant LLM as LLMClient → Gemini
  participant Engine as engine / scenarios / counterfactual
  participant Explain as explain (claims, templates)
  participant DB as SQLite

  User->>Web: Start, read privacy and data-mode notice, choose analyses
  Web->>API: POST /sessions
  API->>DB: create session (token hashed, data_mode recorded)
  API-->>Web: session_id, token, data_mode

  par Track 2: offer
    User->>Web: upload contract (or type terms)
    Web->>API: POST /documents
    API->>Docs: data-mode gate, validate, text layer, redact
    Docs->>LLM: extraction (inline, label, value, page, quote)
    LLM-->>Docs: LoanDocumentExtraction
    Docs->>Docs: deterministic TILA reader
    Docs->>Engine: F00 / F01 / F05 checks
    Docs-->>API: terms with checks (or conflicts, offer chooser)
    API->>DB: store terms, delete raw file
  and Track 1: household intake
    loop until selected analyses are available
      Web->>API: GET /next-question
      API->>Intake: readiness from engine required_inputs
      Intake-->>API: blocking question (or null + refinements)
      API-->>Web: question + why_we_ask + readiness
      User->>Web: answer / skip / decline / estimate
      Web->>API: POST /answers
      opt free text and data_mode = paid
        API->>LLM: parse (whitelisted keys)
        LLM-->>API: facts or malformed → typed widget
      end
      API->>DB: append facts
    end
  end

  Web->>API: GET /documents/{doc_id}
  API-->>Web: verification table
  User->>Web: confirm / edit / choose offer
  Web->>API: POST /documents/{doc_id}/verify
  API-->>Web: LoanOffer ready, readiness updated

  Web->>API: POST /analysis (Idempotency-Key)
  API->>Engine: compute (F00–F14), paired scenarios, counterfactuals
  Engine-->>API: results
  API->>Explain: build claims, templates, key points
  Explain-->>API: ExplanationSection[] (no LLM)
  API->>DB: store DecisionReport
  API-->>Web: DecisionReport
  Web-->>User: key points first, then sections with provenance and verification chips

  User->>Web: delete my data
  Web->>API: DELETE /sessions/{id}
  API->>DB: purge all rows for the session
